<title>JAPAN: NYMEX, HKFE close to ACCESS futures trading link.</title>
<headline>NYMEX, HKFE close to ACCESS futures trading link.</headline>
<dateline>KOBE, Japan 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Futures Exchange (HKFE) will soon start trading New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) products on NYMEX's ACCESS electronic trading system, said John Moore, chairman of NYMEX's COMEX division.</p>
<p>&quot;We will soon be up and running with our electronic trading out of Hong Kong. We've got a lot of interest there,&quot; he said in an interview.</p>
<p>He said that, although trading was not expected to begin before June at the very earliest, the scheduled transfer of the British colony to Chinese sovereignty on July 1 would not interfere with the exchanges' plans.  </p>
<p>He said HKFE was expected to begin with 17 terminals on ACCESS, while the greatest interest appeared to be focused on NYMEX's gold and crude oil contracts.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
